      "claim": "New L2 records show the gallopamil L1 value of 96.3% is not the accepted outcome; single-dose F was 15%, repeated-dose 22.6%, and absolute F 15-23%, so this context now straddles the threshold and no longer strongly supports high.",
      "card_ids": ["C31", "C32", "C42", "C23"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Related basic drugs support F >= 20%: drotaverine 58.2%, bevantolol 57-60%, vernakalant 58-71%, and human ketotifen about 50%; the rabbit ketotifen value of 8% is species-mismatched and not transferable.",
      "card_ids": ["C01", "C08", "C10", "C36", "C16", "C19", "C33", "C37", "C41", "C35"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Verapamil cirrhosis L2 records mostly confirm elevated F of 38-81.5% with one 22% outlier; no L2 record affirmatively places the verapamil class below 20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C21", "C24", "C27", "C28", "C30", "C38", "C39", "C40", "C43", "C34"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "The lowest relevant mean values (verapamil fasted 22%, gallopamil 15-23%) straddle the threshold, so the high prediction is retained but with reduced strength.",
      "card_ids": ["C17", "C31", "C32"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "associated_nonvoting_records",
      "applicability": "high",
      "direction": "contradictory",
      "decision_effect": "weakened",
      "card_ids": ["C21", "C22", "C23", "C24", "C25", "C26", "C27", "C28", "C29", "C30", "C31", "C32", "C33", "C34", "C35", "C36", "C37", "C38", "C39", "C40", "C41", "C42", "C43"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct oral bioavailability measurement exists for the exact query molecule.",
    "The gallopamil context straddles the threshold (15-23%), so the closest analog class is borderline.",
    "Verapamil fasted F range (17-29%) includes values below 20%.",
    "The effect of the benzazepinone lactam on first-pass metabolism relative to the acyclic nitrile analogs is unknown.",
    "No query-specific absorption, solubility, dissolution, or formulation data are available."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted high (F >= 20%) because the most transferable verapamil fasted context has mean F of 22% and verapamil SR and cirrhosis contexts give 34-52%; new L2 records correct gallopamil from 96.3% to 15-23%, which straddles the threshold and weakens but does not overturn the high prediction, since no affirmative threshold-relevant evidence coherently places the query class below 20%."
}

